    "post_id": 68472,
    "title": "כִּי יָשִׂישׂ | Ki Yasis — an ofan piyyuṭ for Tu b’Av by Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
    "author": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
    "coauthors": [
        {
            "name": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
            "bio": "From a family of musicians, Isaac Gantwerk Mayer believes that creative art is one of the most powerful ways to get in touch with the divine. He composes music and poetry in Hebrew and English. (He also <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=342\">translates</a> and <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=820\">transcribes</a> Hebrew and Aramaic texts, adding <em>niqqud</em> and <em>t'amim</em> as needed.) Isaac runs a Jewish music transcription service, which will transcribe and set any Jewish music in any language, recorded or written. Contact his service on <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/pg/isaacgmayerjewishtranscription/\">Facebook</a> or via <a href=\"https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com/contact\">his music blog</a>.",
            "website": "https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com",
            "avatar": "https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/isaac-gantwerk-mayer-2021-e1674561264977-96x96.jpg",
            "profile_link": "https://opensiddur.org/profile/isaac-gantwerk-mayer"
        }
    ],
    "date": "2026-07-28",
    "last_updated": "2026-07-28",
    "excerpt": "An ofan for Tu b’Av, the second part of an intended cycle of yotsrot. Structured around Hosea 11:1 and Ezekiel 3:12, and focusing on the bridal love between Israel and God as well as the corresponding of Israel's and angelic hymning. Written in honor of my friend Eliran’s anniversary.",
    "content": "<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">\nAn ofan for Tu b’Av, the second part of an intended cycle of yotsrot. Structured around Hosea 11:1 and Ezekiel 3:12, and focusing on the bridal love between Israel and God as well as the corresponding of Israel&#8217;s and angelic hymning. Written in honor of my friend Eliran’s anniversary.</p>\n<p>The first word of each line is from Hosea 11:1. In the translation <span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">these words are colored blue</span>. Note that in the original verse, the “them” of line four (literally: him) refers to Israel, not God, but here its context is shifted.</p>\n<p>The first word of the second half of each line is from Ezekiel 3:12, the verse which is recited immediately after an ofan. In the translation <span style=\"color: red;\">these words are colored red</span>. Note that the actual words recited after an ofan are not included here, only the opening portion of the verse.</p>\n<p>Each line ends with either the word “holy,” “blessed,” or, in the last verse, both. In the translation, <span style=\"color: magenta;\">these words are colored magenta</span>.\n</div>\n<hr />\n<table style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" class=\"draggable toggleable-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th id=\"x\" style=\"text-align: right;\">Source (Hebrew)</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Translation (English)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">כִּ֛י</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">יָ</span>שִׂישׂ עָלָי כְּחָתָן הַמָּקוֹם<br />\n<span style=\"color: red;\">וַתִּשָּׂאֵ֣נִי</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">צׇ</span>הֳלָתִי לְמָקוֹם <span style=\"color: magenta;\">קָדוֹשׁ</span>׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"romanized-transliteration\" lang=\"heb-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">As</span> <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Place</span> rejoices over me like a groom;<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[1]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Find Isaiah 62:5&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nmy joy <span style=\"color: red;\">carried me</span> to a <span style=\"color: magenta;\">holy</span> place.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">נַ֥עַר</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">ח</span>מוּד וְנַעֲרַת תִּפְאֶֽרֶת<br />\n<span style=\"color: red;\">ר֔וּחַ</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">קְ</span>דוֹשָׁה אוֹמֶֽרֶת <span style=\"color: magenta;\">בָּרוּךְ</span>׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"romanized-transliteration\" lang=\"heb-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">A</span> pleasant <span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">lad</span>, and a splendid lass; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\na <span style=\"color: red;\">spirit</span> of holiness says, “<span style=\"color: magenta;\">blessed</span>.”\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">ה</span>וּא עַם מְשׁוֹרְרִים<br />\n<span style=\"color: red;\">וָאֶשְׁמַ֣ע</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">רַ</span>בְרְבֵי מַֽעַל מְזַמְּרִים <span style=\"color: magenta;\">קָדוֹשׁ</span>׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"romanized-transliteration\" lang=\"heb-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">Israel</span> is a nation of songsters, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n<span style=\"color: red;\">and I heard</span> the princes on high hymning, “<span style=\"color: magenta;\">holy</span>.”\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">וָאֹהֲבֵ֑הוּ</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">אַ</span>ף־עַל־פִּי כׇּל־צַֽעַר<br />\n<span style=\"color: red;\">אַחֲרַ֔י</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">לִ</span>פְתֹּֽחַ אֶת־הַשַּֽׁעַר <span style=\"color: magenta;\">בָּרוּךְ</span>׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"romanized-transliteration\" lang=\"heb-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">And I loved <span class=\"divine-referent\">Them</span></span> despite all the pain, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n<span style=\"color: red;\">after me</span>! to open the <span style=\"color: magenta;\">blessed</span> gate.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[2]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> The gate of heaven, which is opened from the prayer of those in distress.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">וּמִמִּצְרַ֖יִם</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">חֻ</span>זַּק הָרַֽעַם<br />\n<span style=\"color: red;\">ק֖וֹל</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">זִ</span>קְנֵי עַם <span style=\"color: magenta;\">קָדוֹשׁ</span>׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"romanized-transliteration\" lang=\"heb-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">And from Egypt</span> the thunder was strengthened, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nthe <span style=\"color: red;\">voice</span> of the elders of the <span style=\"color: magenta;\">holy</span> people.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">קָרָ֥אתִי</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">קְ</span>רָא זֶה אֶל־זֶה<br />\n<span style=\"color: red;\">רַ֣עַשׁ</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">אֵ</span>ל רָאָה חוֹזֶה <span style=\"color: magenta;\">בָּרוּךְ</span>׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"romanized-transliteration\" lang=\"heb-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">I called</span>, “Call one to another!”<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[3]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> A reference to Isaiah 6:3 and Isaiah 40:6&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n<span class=\"divine-referent\">Divine</span> <span style=\"color: red;\">tumult</span> a <span style=\"color: magenta;\">blessed</span> prophet saw.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">לִבְנִֽי</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">מְ</span>כֻנֶּה יְשֻׁרוּן<br />\n<span style=\"color: red;\">גָּד֑וֹל</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">נָ</span>שִֽׁירָה לוֹ מוּל יְשִׁירוּן <span style=\"color: magenta;\">קָדוֹשׁ</span> וּ<span style=\"color: magenta;\">בָרוּךְ</span>׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"romanized-transliteration\" lang=\"heb-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n&#8220;<span style=\"color: dodgerblue;\">My son</span>” Jeshurun is called; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n<span style=\"color: red;\">great</span>! Let us sing while they sing<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[4]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> According to the heikhalot mystic corpus, very influential on the structure of ofanim, Israel and the angels pray at the same time.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> “<span style=\"color: magenta;\">holy</span> and <span style=\"color: magenta;\">blessed</span>.”\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"speaker-mute footnotes_reference_container\"> <div class=\"footnote_container_prepare\"><p><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_label pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\">Notes</span><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_collapse_button\" style=\"display: none;; display: none;\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\"></span></p></div> <div id=\"footnote_references_container__1\" style=\"\"><table class=\"footnotes_table footnote-reference-container\"><caption class=\"accessibility\">Notes</caption> <tbody> \r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >1</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Find Isaiah 62:5</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >2</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">The gate of heaven, which is opened from the prayer of those in distress.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >3</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">A reference to Isaiah 6:3 and Isaiah 40:6</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >4</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">According to the heikhalot mystic corpus, very influential on the structure of ofanim, Israel and the angels pray at the same time.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n </tbody> </table> </div></div><script type=\"text/javascript\"> function footnote_expand_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').show(); jQuery('#footnote_reference_container_collapse_button__1').text('−'); } function footnote_collapse_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').hide(); jQuery('#footnote_reference_container_collapse_button__1').text('+'); } function footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1() { if (jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').is(':hidden')) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); } else { footnote_collapse_reference_container__1(); } } function footnote_moveToReference__1(p_str_TargetID) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); var l_obj_Target = jQuery('#' + p_str_TargetID); if (l_obj_Target.length) { jQuery( 'html, body' ).delay( 0 ); jQuery('html, body').animate({ scrollTop: l_obj_Target.offset().top - window.innerHeight * 0.2 }, 380); } } function footnote_moveToAnchor__1(p_str_TargetID) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); var l_obj_Target = jQuery('#' + p_str_TargetID); if (l_obj_Target.length) { jQuery( 'html, body' ).delay( 0 ); jQuery('html, body').animate({ scrollTop: l_obj_Target.offset().top - window.innerHeight * 0.2 }, 380); } }</script>",
